1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
This asshole turned a five hundred dollar loan into almost two grand.

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:08,180
Who is he? Scott Tucker, who ran online payday loans out of Kansas.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:12,520
Payday loan means you borrow a little cash, then pay it back on your next paycheck.

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,640
Who takes those? People who are broke till Friday.

5
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:19,020
His paperwork said: borrow five hundred, pay back six hundred fifty.

6
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,020
Double-tap if you've ever signed some shit without reading it.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,880
Here's the trick. The loan renewed itself every damn payday.

8
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:31,520
Each time, he took a hundred fifty in fees, and your five hundred never went down.

9
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,840
So you're paying rent on your own debt, every two weeks.

10
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:41,320
One borrower the Justice Department described paid nineteen hundred twenty-five dollars on that five hundred dollar loan.

11
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,920
Prosecutors put the rate around seven hundred percent a year.

12
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:48,020
Send this to whoever thinks payday loans are no big deal.

13
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:51,180
At least four and a half million people got hit with these.

14
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:54,360
He pulled in more than three and a half billion dollars.

15
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,960
And he spent some of it on his own race car team.

16
00:00:57,380 --> 00:01:02,160
And when states came for him? He hid behind Native American tribes, claiming they owned it.

17
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,660
Why tribes? 'Cause states can't sue them.

18
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,600
But prosecutors called it a sham.

19
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,280
Follow, 'cause karma finally showed up.

20
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:14,040
He got arrested in twenty sixteen, and a jury convicted him on all fourteen counts.

21
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:18,980
He was sentenced to two hundred fucking months in prison, more than sixteen years.

22
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:22,200
Fine print: read it or skip it? One word.

